# Workflow: audits, item IDs and "continue"

Amit writes prompts in a separate assistant (Grok Bot) and pastes them here. Prompts are often short, in Hindi/Hinglish or English, e.g. "continue", "VDB-03 karo", "MST-05 fix karo", "next item".

## Audit and plan files (`docs/audits/`)
| File | Scope | ID prefix |
|------|-------|-----------|
| `docs/audits/vector-db-preaudit.md` | Knowledge engine / vector DB | `VDB-xx` |
| `docs/audits/masters-gap-audit.md` | Masters (Client, IS Code, Products/Services, Test Parameter, Equipment, GST, Units ...) | `MST-xx` |
| `docs/audits/finance-module-plan.md` (later) | Finance module | `FIN-xx` |

Each item has: **ID**, title, priority (P0–P3), status (`Open` / `In progress` / `Done` / `Blocked` / `Won't fix`), affected files, problem with evidence (file:line), fix plan, acceptance criteria, and a notes/log line.

## When asked to work on an ID or to "continue"
1. Open the relevant audit file. With no ID given, take the highest-priority `Open` (or `In progress`) item in the file under discussion. If it's unclear which file is meant, ask one short question.
2. Read the item's acceptance criteria and inspect the code it references.
3. Post a short plan of 3–6 bullets, then implement the **smallest change** that meets the criteria. Do one ID per run unless asked for more. Split a large item into sub-IDs (`VDB-03a`, `VDB-03b`) inside the file.
4. Verify: lint, typecheck or build for the frontend, `node --check` for functions, test modules and evals for `knowledge_engine`. A SQL migration is written but not applied unless Amit asks.
5. Update the item in the audit file: status, date (YYYY-MM-DD), files changed, verification commands and results, follow-ups.
   - Mark `Done` only when verification passed.
   - Use `Blocked` with a reason when the item needs a production migration, a deploy, a business decision or data Amit must provide.
6. Finish with the summary (see core rule) and suggest the next ID.

## Creating or extending an audit
- Back findings with evidence (file paths, line numbers, query results). Don't invent issues. Never renumber existing IDs; append new ones.
- Domain references for BIS rules: bis.gov.in, manakonline.in, standards.bis.gov.in, lims.bis.gov.in. Use them for research. Don't add scraping of these sites to the app without asking; portal automation lives in `extensions/`.

## Business naming (always)
- Write **"Quality International Research & Laboratories Private Limited"** in full. Never use "Pvt Ltd", "Pvt. Ltd." or "P. Ltd." anywhere: UI text, seeds, templates, emails, PDFs, docs.
- Q Engineering is the consultancy brand (`qengineering.in`). Company names in client data stay exactly as the client registered them.
